dgame migration. While we do not support the NewStable token, we continue to support the ERC-20 version of DAI. Customers can still deposit, withdraw, and trade DAI.\" }","id":"30000002625","key":"DAI","type":"string","subType":"json"},{"defaultValue":"{ \"message\": \"Gemini is aware of the FTM to S migration. While we do not support the new S token, we continue to support the ERC-20 version of FTM. Customers can still deposit, withdraw, and trade FTM.\" }","id":"30000002626","key":"FTM","type":"string","subType":"json"},{"defaultValue":"{ \"message\": \"Gemini is aware of the FET to ASI migration. While we do not support the new ASI token, we continue to support the ERC-20 version of FET. Customers can still deposit, withdraw, and trade FET.\" }","id":"30000002627","key":"FET","type":"string","subType":"json"},{"defaultValue":"{\"message\":\"Gemini is aware of the MATIC to POL migration. While we do not support the new POL token, we continue to support the ERC-20 version of MATIC. Customers can still deposit, withdraw, trade, and stake MATIC (where available). \\n\\nIf you prefer, you may withdraw your MATIC tokens to a self-hosted wallet to complete the migration manually. Any updates or changes to these features will be communicated through Gemini's official channels as soon as they are available.\"}","id":"30000002628","key":"MATIC","type":"string","subType":"json"},{"defaultValue":"{ \"message\": \"Gemini is aware of the RNDR to RENDER migration. While we do not support the new RENDER token, we continue to support the ERC-20 version of RNDR. Customers can still deposit, withdraw, and trade RNDR. \\n\\nIf you prefer, you may withdraw your RNDR tokens to a self-hosted wallet to complete the migration manually. Any updates or changes to these features will be communicated through Gemini's official channels as soon as they are available.\" }","id":"30000002629","key":"RNDR","type":"string","subType":"json"},{"defaultValue":"{ \"message\": \"Gemini does not intend 